{"id":27,"name":"sandshrew","speciesId":27,"dex":27,"form":"normal","generation":1,"types":["ground"],"stats":{"hp":50,"attack":75,"defense":85,"special-attack":20,"special-defense":30,"speed":40},"abilities":[{"name":"sand-veil","hidden":false},{"name":"sand-rush","hidden":true}],"height":6,"weight":120,"baseExp":60,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/27.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/27.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/27.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/27.ogg","genus":"Mouse Pokémon","genusPt":"Pokémon rato","flavor":[{"version":"red","text":"Burrows deep underground in arid locations far from water. It only emerges to hunt for food."},{"version":"yellow","text":"Its body is dry. When it gets cold at night, its hide is said to become coated with a fine dew."},{"version":"gold","text":"If it fell from a great height, this POKéMON could save itself by rolling into a ball and bouncing."},{"version":"silver","text":"Disliking water, it lives in deep burrows in arid areas. It can roll itself instantly into a ball."},{"version":"crystal","text":"It prefers dry, sandy places because it uses the sand to protect itself when threatened."},{"version":"ruby","text":"SANDSHREW’s body is configured to absorb water without waste, enabling it to survive in an arid desert. This POKéMON curls up to protect itself from its enemies."},{"version":"sapphire","text":"SANDSHREW has a very dry hide that is extremely tough. The POKéMON can roll into a ball that repels any attack. At night, it burrows into the desert sand to sleep."},{"version":"emerald","text":"When it curls up in a ball, it can make any attack bounce off harmlessly. Its hide has turned tough and solid as a result of living in the desert."},{"version":"